1
00:00:08,560 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and try stepping back,
will you?

2
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:24,260
Anyone without money, come to my place.

3
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:29,000
I don't have any either, but don't worry.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,800
Look at the blue sky,

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:36,300
the white clouds.

6
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:42,820
Somehow, it'll all work out in time.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,900
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

8
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,540
I don't have any either, so don't worry.

9
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:45,140
It's already been a year since
we entered the 21st century.

10
00:01:45,780 --> 00:01:48,640
Yet crime shows no sign of disappearing.

11
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:51,240
No, if anything, it just keeps increasing.

12
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:56,940
Our Special Investigations Division has been responding
with everything we've got to the crime that grows every day.

13
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:04,200
But our capacity to cope
is nearing its limit.

14
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:15,280
So we've decided to add a new
special detective to the force.

15
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:18,420
And his name is...

16
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:21,660
Invisible Cop Anawaru!

17
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:29,300
That's why we're appointing
you as a special detective.

18
00:02:31,044 --> 00:02:35,880
I've told you,
I don't want to be teamed up with perverts!

19
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:39,560
What? My...

20
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:43,860
Where's the pervert in that?

21
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,620
That's exactly it!

22
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:50,040
What's the point of wearing nothing but swim
trunks or a sailor suit and striking weird poses?!

23
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:55,460
Then rest assured, we won't need
a new uniform this time either.

24
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:58,520
You can strike any pose you like.

25
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:04,960
Because you're going to become invisible.

26
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:06,900
Invisible man?

27
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:13,540
What the hell is this?

28
00:03:24,580 --> 00:03:26,260
Professor Esaki

29
00:03:26,260 --> 00:03:29,300
Ryo-san, could this be...

30
00:03:29,300 --> 00:03:31,400
No doubt about it, it's Pink Lady!

31
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:32,273
Hahaha,

32
00:03:32,323 --> 00:03:37,360
when Japanese people hear
"invisible man," the first thing they think of is Pink Lady!

33
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:40,980
But that song is "UFO," isn't it!

34
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:41,600
Gulp!

35
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:49,000
R-right! Actually, I just can't remember the intro to
"Invisible Man"!

36
00:03:49,840 --> 00:03:51,620
What on earth did you come here for!

37
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:56,040
Invisible Liquid

38
00:03:58,600 --> 00:04:03,100
By drinking this liquid,
you can become an invisible man.

39
00:04:03,980 --> 00:04:07,100
And you'll become the Special
Detective Invisible Cop!

40
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:10,100
No way!
First of all, did you test it properly?

41
00:04:10,260 --> 00:04:13,200
D-don't worry about such small details.

42
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:16,120
In other words, I'm the guinea pig, right?

43
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:19,200
Honestly,
these guys are outrageous every single time.

44
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:25,103
Ryotsu,

45
00:04:25,153 --> 00:04:29,720
Looks like you have no choice but
to become an invisible detective.

46
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:30,440
What?!

47
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:32,800
Ryo-chan's body is...

48
00:04:33,960 --> 00:04:35,300
b-becoming see-through!

49
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:36,220
What?

50
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:43,160
While you were outside a moment ago,

51
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:52,640
we put the invisible liquid we got
from Professor Esaki into your teacup.

52
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:56,760
That was a flawless teamwork play.

53
00:04:56,760 --> 00:04:58,280
That's dirty, you bastards!

54
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:00,720
It's to wipe out crime.

55
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:01,860
It can't be helped.

56
00:05:01,860 --> 00:05:04,680
You're basically criminals yourselves!

57
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,960
Senpai's body...

58
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:10,620
disappeared.

59
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:14,180
I've never seen an invisible man before.

60
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:15,720
Well, I can't actually see him, though.

61
00:05:20,280 --> 00:05:21,540
My body...

62
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:23,760
That's right! Are you that happy?

63
00:05:23,920 --> 00:05:26,200
Does this face look happy to you?!

64
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:29,220
You can't see it. It's invisible, after all.

65
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:30,100
What?

66
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:34,300
Ryotsu, from the moment you're officially
assigned as a special detective,

67
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,520
your salary will triple from what it was.

68
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:41,280
On top of that, you'll get a
special allowance for every dispatch.

69
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:42,900
And you'll receive a position allowance too.

70
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:46,240
Do you really think I'll be
fooled by such sweet words?

71
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,660
He's definitely grinning right now.

72
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:50,380
No doubt about it.

73
00:05:51,620 --> 00:05:53,900
You two shouldn't be able
to see my face, right?

74
00:05:53,900 --> 00:05:56,040
Even if we can't see it, we know.

75
00:05:57,580 --> 00:05:58,660
Settled, then.

76
00:05:58,660 --> 00:06:00,000
Then take your clothes off.

77
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:04,480
If you're still wearing clothes,
what's the point of being an invisible man?

78
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:06,000
Th-that's true.

79
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,740
Fine, fine.

80
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:09,300
Guess I just take them off, then.

81
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:10,380
Take them off.

82
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,620
Even what's inside is transparent.

83
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:17,420
Don't stare at me like that.

84
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:19,420
I can't see a thing, you know.

85
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:22,340
Hey, do I really have to take this off too?

86
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:23,780
Of course.

87
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:26,180
Even though I know I won't be seen,

88
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:28,660
taking off my underwear in
front of people makes me uneasy.

89
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:31,500
How about this?

90
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:35,240
When an invisible detective
carries out a mission,

91
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,460
he must always be completely naked.

92
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:40,160
That's why he has to be tough
against both heat and cold,

93
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:43,080
so you were chosen because you
look like you'd never catch a cold.

94
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:45,300
I thought as much.

95
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:50,100
It's me.

96
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:50,920
Yeah.

97
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,040
Uh-huh.

98
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,580
Got it.

99
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:54,760
I'll be right back.

100
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:56,740
The salary came through.

101
00:06:56,740 --> 00:06:58,480
Invisible Detective Ryo Tour

102
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:01,100
Until you're officially assigned to
the Special Investigations Division,

103
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:04,040
keep doing your regular police box duties.

104
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:05,120
Well then.

105
00:07:07,020 --> 00:07:09,140
I should be heading out too.

106
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,140
Hold on a second!

107
00:07:10,140 --> 00:07:12,960
How do I get my body back to normal?

108
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:16,900
I only just became invisible!

109
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:19,320
There's no need to worry
about changing back yet.

110
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:22,340
That's exactly why I'm worried,
since you made it!

111
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:27,140
If winter has come,
can spring be far behind?

112
00:07:27,820 --> 00:07:30,320
Everything has a beginning and an end.

113
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:34,860
Even the greatest invention
eventually wears off.

114
00:07:34,860 --> 00:07:39,660
So you're saying all I can do is wait
for it to wear off and go back to normal?

115
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:44,480
Only God knows that.

116
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:44,880
What?

117
00:07:44,880 --> 00:07:45,080
What?

118
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:47,940
Contact me once you're back to normal,
won't you?

119
00:07:47,990 --> 00:07:49,960
Relaxun. Well then, farewell!

120
00:07:54,820 --> 00:07:55,920
For crying out loud.

121
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,040
Are you laughing?

122
00:07:57,540 --> 00:08:01,235
He's furious!
After all these years of putting up with me,

123
00:08:01,285 --> 00:08:03,860
can't you even tell if I'm angry or crying?

124
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:06,640
But we can't see your expression.

125
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:08,960
What kind of face were you making?

126
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:11,620
You two are so exasperating.

127
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:16,000
Mm.

128
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:17,120
Mm.

129
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:17,320
Mm.

130
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:17,940
Mm.

131
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:21,200
I was making this face.

132
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:24,640
I see.

133
00:08:25,820 --> 00:08:26,540
"I see" is not the point.

134
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,560
Make an effort to see with your mind's eye!

135
00:08:28,960 --> 00:08:30,120
Oh, y-yes.

136
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,020
Got it?

137
00:08:33,180 --> 00:08:35,420
I'm standing right in front of you now.

138
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:36,400
Look closely.

139
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:38,420
I'm going to laugh.

140
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,060
Well? Can you see me?

141
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,380
How am I supposed to know?

142
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:47,100
Well? How about now?

143
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:53,180
Now that you mention it, I think I
could kind of see something, Reiko-san.

144
00:08:53,180 --> 00:08:55,300
Hehe, just a little.

145
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:58,840
Alright, this time I'm going to get angry.
How about that?

146
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:03,320
This time I could definitely see it, right?

147
00:09:03,320 --> 00:09:04,480
Y-yeah, sure.

148
00:09:04,480 --> 00:09:07,520
Then guess what kind of
face I'm making this time.

149
00:09:11,140 --> 00:09:14,620
Well, how should I put this?

150
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,260
Well...

151
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:19,050
There are eyes, and there's a nose,

152
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:21,940
there's a mouth, and there are ears...

153
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:24,860
L-look! I can see the nose!
He's smiling, right!

154
00:09:25,700 --> 00:09:27,280
Wagaman! It's me, I'm behind you!

155
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,460
That's cheating, that's...

156
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:31,760
Good morning!

157
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:32,660
Chief!

158
00:09:33,060 --> 00:09:34,100
Good morning!

159
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:34,420
Good morning.

160
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,920
What, is Ryotsu skipping work again?

161
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,680
No Ryo-san is...

162
00:09:40,680 --> 00:09:42,760
Just be quiet.

163
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,600
I'll make some tea.

164
00:09:45,600 --> 00:09:47,040
Thanks.

165
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:50,800
Honestly, that Ryotsu...
he's a hopeless case.

166
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:54,880
But first I need the toilet.

167
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:02,660
That Chief, he's so incredibly lucky.

168
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:09,140
Remember this. I finally became invisible,
so I'm going to make the Chief pay for it.

169
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:15,260
When I'm back to normal, I'll trip you up.
Senpai, you'd better not.

170
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:19,880
Shut up! Listen, you two, keep quiet.
I don't know anything about it.

171
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:28,320
Aaaah, that feels great. I feel so light,
like my body's gotten lighter.

172
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,240
Did I just hear some weird noise?

173
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:36,040
Is there a rat or something around here?

174
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:39,240
No, Chief, actually...

175
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:41,640
Chase it away with my fighting spirit!

176
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:42,960
Amazing.

177
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:50,440
Please stop it.

178
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:54,540
I thought I just heard Ryotsu's voice.

179
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:56,760
It must be your imagination.

180
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,840
It's your imagination! Nothing of the sort!

181
00:11:00,060 --> 00:11:02,720
The one you're hitting right now is me!

182
00:11:03,280 --> 00:11:05,680
I've become an invisible man!

183
00:11:07,700 --> 00:11:09,080
Is that really true, Chief?

184
00:11:09,420 --> 00:11:12,660
Senpai has become a special detective
in the Special Investigation Division!

185
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:17,780
I knew that! I got a notice too!

186
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,880
That's cruel!
If you knew, why didn't you say so?

187
00:11:21,260 --> 00:11:22,380
I knew all along!

188
00:11:22,900 --> 00:11:25,460
Pulling the chair out from under
me to make me fall on my butt,

189
00:11:25,460 --> 00:11:28,360
or sticking a foot out to trip me, too.

190
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:30,960
You noticed all that?

191
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:36,760
I can imagine exactly
what you're going to do.

192
00:11:36,760 --> 00:11:38,520
Please don't pull my ear.

193
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:41,260
You certainly know where my ears are.

194
00:11:41,620 --> 00:11:44,920
I can see through all of
Ryotsu's behavior patterns.

195
00:11:44,920 --> 00:11:48,680
After all,
I've been your superior for over 20 years.

196
00:11:49,740 --> 00:11:51,560
As expected of Chief Ohara.

197
00:11:52,380 --> 00:11:54,260
Chief, your tea is ready.

198
00:11:54,480 --> 00:11:55,380
Ah

199
00:11:55,380 --> 00:11:58,680
Chachachacha! Watch it, Reiko! Honestly!

200
00:11:59,520 --> 00:12:01,900
I can't see you, so what do you expect?

201
00:12:02,260 --> 00:12:06,960
Damn it! That's why I said
I didn't want to be invisible!

202
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:10,885
Ugh,

203
00:12:10,935 --> 00:12:15,760
Damn! I'm late again!

204
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:20,740
Whoa! My face is gone! It's gone!

205
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:23,760
My body's gone too.

206
00:12:23,760 --> 00:12:26,040
Did I die or something?

207
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:31,400
Right, that's right.

208
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,700
So I did become an invisible detective,
didn't I?

209
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:35,520
I'd completely forgotten.

210
00:12:36,540 --> 00:12:38,400
You idiot!

211
00:12:40,940 --> 00:12:43,340
You're late again, Ryotsu!

212
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:46,160
Sorry, sorry.

213
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:49,220
If you start slacking off on your
work just because you're invisible,

214
00:12:49,220 --> 00:12:50,740
you'll be fired, got it?

215
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:53,180
Tea's ready.

216
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:57,700
Ah that's why! I told you to be careful!

217
00:12:58,260 --> 00:13:00,740
But we can't see him,
so what else can we do!

218
00:13:01,140 --> 00:13:02,400
Mmmmm...

219
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:07,020
Damn it! Becoming an invisible
detective hasn't done me any good at all!

220
00:13:07,740 --> 00:13:09,660
Oh yeah...

221
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:14,260
Here you go, Ryotsu!

222
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:16,660
Ryotsu!

223
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:27,977
He's not here... heh heh,

224
00:13:28,027 --> 00:13:30,920
Ryotsu, he's not here. Ryotsu.

225
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:32,200
What's wrong?

226
00:13:33,160 --> 00:13:35,760
Ryotsu's gone somehow, without us noticing.

227
00:13:36,200 --> 00:13:37,780
Looks like the senior officer got you.

228
00:13:37,780 --> 00:13:40,000
Damn Ryotsu.

229
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:43,020
What's with that pile of boiled eggs?

230
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:47,420
Well, I got a lot of eggs
from the neighboring farm.

231
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:49,340
Here it is.

232
00:13:50,200 --> 00:13:52,400
Oh no, I forgot my wallet.

233
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:54,420
I can't even play pachinko like this.

234
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:56,620
I wonder if the Chief is still here?

235
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:00,020
Heh heh, nobody's here!

236
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:03,580
Ryo-chan!

237
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:05,980
Where have you been all this time!

238
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,800
Chief, you can see me?

239
00:14:09,100 --> 00:14:11,200
I can see right through you!

240
00:14:13,900 --> 00:14:16,960
So that's it.
You figured it out from this eggshell

241
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:20,560
If you really want to go outside that badly,
I'll let you.

242
00:14:21,820 --> 00:14:24,160
Take these papers to the station.

243
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:26,880
Yeah, yeah, I get it.

244
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,420
I'm heading out!

245
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:32,820
Damn the Chief,
there was no need to get so angry.

246
00:14:33,460 --> 00:14:34,360
Out of the way! Move!

247
00:14:36,020 --> 00:14:39,060
What's that? A remote-controlled bicycle?

248
00:14:39,700 --> 00:14:41,840
Move, and quit gawking at me!

249
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:45,520
Ow ow ow ow ow

250
00:14:58,320 --> 00:14:58,940
Aaaaah!

251
00:14:58,940 --> 00:15:00,280
I've been through hell.

252
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:06,560
It's broken, but it can't be helped.

253
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,600
Let's walk.

254
00:15:15,780 --> 00:15:17,100
That Amida just now...

255
00:15:17,100 --> 00:15:17,880
Amida, Amida.

256
00:15:17,880 --> 00:15:19,640
What was that just now?

257
00:15:20,520 --> 00:15:22,600
I don't know about that sort of thing, but

258
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:26,300
It seems we're definitely pretty worn out.

259
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:29,300
We've been overworking.
We're not taking a break, not even a little!

260
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:30,100
What?

261
00:15:34,620 --> 00:15:37,440
That was close, it grazed my shoulder!

262
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:39,720
They can't see me, after all.

263
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:45,060
Did I hear someone's voice?

264
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,260
Oh well.

265
00:15:51,060 --> 00:15:54,480
The road with cars is dangerous,
let's take the back street.

266
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,680
This way looks safe enough.

267
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:00,840
Ow ow ow

268
00:16:01,260 --> 00:16:02,620
I stepped on a nail.

269
00:16:02,620 --> 00:16:05,020
Walking on my own isn't
something you should do.

270
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:05,580
This

271
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:07,500
came out

272
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:09,060
Hey!

273
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:14,540
What's with this dog? Can it see me?

274
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:17,340
So dogs can tell by smell

275
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:19,780
Get away!

276
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,080
That hurts!

277
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,000
Kekeke! Don't bite my butt!

278
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:30,560
Shut up! You stupid mutt!

279
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,560
Damn it! It got all over me!

280
00:16:34,380 --> 00:16:36,300
Aw, the envelope's soaked too.

281
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:42,140
It hurts! Look at this!

282
00:16:44,360 --> 00:16:47,420
How many times have I told you,
no playing soccer in the alley!

283
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:51,120
Back alleys are full of danger too.

284
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,280
Finally made it.

285
00:16:57,820 --> 00:17:01,260
It's from Chief Ohara at the
Kameari Kōen-mae police box.

286
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:02,900
Yes, thank you for your hard work.

287
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:06,780
What the heck is this?

288
00:17:06,780 --> 00:17:09,280
Hey, it's super lame, isn't it?

289
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:11,460
It's Komachi and Naoko.

290
00:17:13,520 --> 00:17:15,000
Is this the women's changing room?

291
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:17,660
I went to the trouble of becoming invisible,
after all.

292
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:22,340
Emergency report: within the
Katsushika Police Station jurisdiction,

293
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:24,500
a hit-and-run incident has occurred.

294
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:27,940
What's wrong?

295
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:30,160
I think I bumped into something...

296
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:32,220
Must be my imagination. Let's go.

297
00:17:32,220 --> 00:17:32,740
Yeah.

298
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,240
Damn it, don't open it so suddenly!

299
00:17:37,240 --> 00:17:39,340
I really smacked my nose.

300
00:17:39,780 --> 00:17:40,400
Let's go.

301
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,720
Your time to shine, Invisible Detective.

302
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:45,060
What are you doing here?

303
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:45,869
Hehehe,

304
00:17:45,919 --> 00:17:50,560
Every man who becomes invisible
wants to sneak in here at least once.

305
00:17:50,980 --> 00:17:52,820
Father-in-law, y-you're being read!

306
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:55,660
Why are you coming out from the inside?

307
00:17:56,300 --> 00:17:58,020
Don't sweat the small stuff.

308
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:00,136
Senior Officer Ryotsu,

309
00:18:00,186 --> 00:18:02,700
for solving this case so brilliantly,

310
00:18:02,700 --> 00:18:05,827
if you're officially hired into
the Special Investigations Division,

311
00:18:05,877 --> 00:18:07,360
your salary will triple!

312
00:18:07,360 --> 00:18:09,980
R-really? Alright, I'm in!

313
00:18:11,780 --> 00:18:15,500
Today, a man who broke into a
financial company in Katsushika Ward

314
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:19,160
was confronted by security guards and police
who rushed there after an emergency call.

315
00:18:19,160 --> 00:18:21,760
He took one female
employee hostage and fled.

316
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,920
He is currently barricaded
inside this new building.

317
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:27,160
The scene is in chaos.

318
00:18:30,840 --> 00:18:32,600
Look, does anyone care?

319
00:18:32,600 --> 00:18:34,760
If you don't bring the
cash and a car right away,

320
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:36,780
don't say I didn't warn you
about what happens to this woman.

321
00:18:36,780 --> 00:18:37,660
Help!

322
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:41,095
We just can't get any closer.
At a time like this,

323
00:18:41,145 --> 00:18:44,960
if only invisible Ryotsu were here,
we could get close to the culprit.

324
00:18:45,220 --> 00:18:48,020
I heard he left Katsushika
Station with Kaipan Deka, but...

325
00:18:48,480 --> 00:18:49,520
He's already here.

326
00:18:50,260 --> 00:18:51,320
Kaipan Deka.

327
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:52,540
I'm here too.

328
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,440
Hey, you, over here!

329
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:56,640
How did you know?

330
00:18:57,140 --> 00:19:01,900
I've told you, I can see right through your behavior patterns!
This is no time to be fooling around!

331
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:03,120
Yes, sorry.

332
00:19:03,780 --> 00:19:04,500
What's the situation?

333
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:08,340
The culprit is a young man,
armed with a gun in each hand.

334
00:19:08,800 --> 00:19:14,420
He's taken a young woman hostage and is demanding
500 million yen in cash and a getaway car.

335
00:19:15,400 --> 00:19:19,200
The building was just completed
and nothing has moved in yet.

336
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:23,700
Because of that, there are few obstacles,
which actually makes it harder to get in.

337
00:19:24,500 --> 00:19:27,520
There's only one entrance,
the front main door.

338
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:32,860
Right, invisible Deka-kun could get
close to the culprit without being noticed.

339
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:36,340
First, rescue the hostage.

340
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:36,760
Yes.

341
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:42,900
Once the hostage's rescue is confirmed, the riot
police will rush in and apprehend the culprit.

342
00:19:42,900 --> 00:19:46,320
Don't worry, I'll give the
culprit a thorough thrashing myself!

343
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:50,080
No, you think only about
rescuing the hostage.

344
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:52,820
When you get carried away,
you always botch things.

345
00:19:53,240 --> 00:19:53,820
Yeah, yeah.

346
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:58,160
Senpai, the culprit locked the building
from the inside when he went in.

347
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:02,160
Here's the spare key.
I borrowed it from the building owner.

348
00:20:02,160 --> 00:20:03,280
Good, understood.

349
00:20:04,500 --> 00:20:08,860
Alright, operation starts now.
Invisible man, copy that. I'm heading out!

350
00:20:13,580 --> 00:20:17,800
I hope he really can't be seen.
Whew, all clear.

351
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:23,800
He's not visible at all. Even with his bare butt showing like that,
nobody would notice.

352
00:20:23,800 --> 00:20:28,760
Has Ryotsu still not reached the entrance?

353
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:32,180
Senpai, looks like he's gone inside.

354
00:20:33,340 --> 00:20:35,400
Infiltration successful.

355
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:36,900
It's on the second floor.

356
00:20:38,140 --> 00:20:40,640
So, rescuing the hostage comes first.

357
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:44,620
Hey! Hurry up! I want a car and money!

358
00:20:47,380 --> 00:20:50,340
Shh, stop looking around like that.
I'm a cop.

359
00:20:50,340 --> 00:20:52,000
I'll save you right now.

360
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,240
What... what is it?

361
00:20:55,720 --> 00:20:58,500
Right when it matters,
the important part is showing!

362
00:20:59,520 --> 00:21:02,160
Even if you cover it with your hand,
your hand is see-through!

363
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:02,940
Hey, you there!

364
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:03,940
Don't move!

365
00:21:03,940 --> 00:21:04,680
Damn it!

366
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:05,740
Stupid woman!

367
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,120
Who the hell are you?

368
00:21:10,120 --> 00:21:12,320
Invisible cop! You're under arrest!

369
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:13,300
Stay back!

370
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:16,140
Okay.

371
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,480
I'll catch you!

372
00:21:19,480 --> 00:21:21,720
Idiot, what are you doing?

373
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,220
He yanked me!

374
00:21:22,220 --> 00:21:24,000
Alright, I'll go in first.

375
00:21:32,680 --> 00:21:35,540
A case that's over is a solved case.

376
00:21:35,540 --> 00:21:36,420
Ryotsu!

377
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:38,640
Senpai!

378
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:40,280
Ryotsu's figure is...

379
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:43,140
It must be that the effects of
the medicine are wearing off.

380
00:21:43,140 --> 00:21:43,760
Excuse me, move aside.

381
00:21:45,120 --> 00:21:47,660
It seems the culprit has just been arrested.

382
00:21:47,660 --> 00:21:50,840
Exclusive scoop! This is the arrest scene.

383
00:21:57,380 --> 00:21:58,280
What was that just now?

384
00:21:58,280 --> 00:21:59,920
The culprit's a pervert

385
00:22:03,740 --> 00:22:06,520
Good thing the hostage woman is safe,
isn't it?

386
00:22:06,520 --> 00:22:08,240
Yeah, but

387
00:22:08,720 --> 00:22:10,080
what wasn't good was

388
00:22:10,600 --> 00:22:11,700
Ryo-chan, wasn't it?

389
00:22:11,700 --> 00:22:15,040
On top of showing his bare
naked self across the nation,

390
00:22:15,040 --> 00:22:16,840
and now that he's no longer invisible,

391
00:22:16,840 --> 00:22:19,300
no assignment to the Special
Investigation Division,

392
00:22:19,300 --> 00:22:21,780
and no special allowance either.

393
00:22:22,960 --> 00:22:25,000
Don't be so down, Gorilla-kun.

394
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:27,960
Everyone makes mistakes, you know.

395
00:22:27,960 --> 00:22:31,240
Hey, Ezagi! This happened because of you!

396
00:22:31,240 --> 00:22:33,740
You made a half-baked potion!

397
00:22:33,740 --> 00:22:37,460
Invisible Liquid Martitz!

398
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:41,940
It's a masterpiece, and this time it's perfect!
Go on, drink it.

399
00:22:41,940 --> 00:22:44,260
I'll never drink anything you make again!

400
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:48,900
It's already in that tea, though.

401
00:22:48,900 --> 00:22:49,540
What?

402
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:53,720
You idiot! I drank it!

403
00:23:25,100 --> 00:23:26,220
What's wrong, senpai?

404
00:23:26,220 --> 00:23:28,380
I'm getting a weird tingling.

405
00:23:28,800 --> 00:23:29,780
Could it be...

406
00:23:33,700 --> 00:23:35,520
What is it, Ryo-san?

407
00:23:35,820 --> 00:23:38,560
Now only the most important
part has turned invisible.

408
00:23:39,920 --> 00:23:41,200
Everyone, take a look.

409
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:43,660
Yeah! Ew, don't show us that!

410
00:23:43,660 --> 00:23:45,960
I'm telling you,
it's disappeared from sight.

411
00:23:46,420 --> 00:23:46,920
Here, see?

412
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:49,740
Well, I'll be.

413
00:23:49,740 --> 00:23:50,520
Is that weird?

414
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:52,680
Damn it! That Ezaki!

415
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:54,094
Oh no...

416
00:23:54,144 --> 00:23:57,860
Yazaki, get back here! What are
you going to do about this of mine?!

417
00:23:58,500 --> 00:24:03,640
Damn it!
I'm so done with being an invisible man!

418
00:24:27,560 --> 00:24:32,000
If I'm dawdling at the corner,

419
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:35,000
the moon runs off, and we're off!

420
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:38,100
because now isn't everything,

421
00:24:38,900 --> 00:24:42,560
don't get too sulky.

422
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:46,300
even if you fudge the truth a little,

423
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:50,460
sometimes you're helping someone.

424
00:24:50,460 --> 00:24:52,480
Baby, do you know me?

425
00:24:52,520 --> 00:24:56,660
Facing tomorrow, a nice spirit,

426
00:24:57,720 --> 00:25:04,240
doing what needs doing,
even the trivial stuff, a cute spirit.

427
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:11,520
Being hard to read is just
because I want to look that way.

428
00:25:12,520 --> 00:25:17,260
It's better than a makeover, right?

429
00:25:18,980 --> 00:25:24,820
Na-na-na-na, na-na-na-na, na-na-na-na

430
00:25:30,220 --> 00:25:33,340
Kankichi, this is terrible!
A baby is being born!

431
00:25:33,820 --> 00:25:36,760
Lemon can't give birth, obviously!

432
00:25:36,760 --> 00:25:39,240
As usual, you're an idiot, Kankichi.

433
00:25:39,780 --> 00:25:43,100
Mom says Lemon is going
to become a big sister.

434
00:25:43,660 --> 00:25:47,260
Next time: Lemon becomes big sister.
See you then!

435
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:51,060
That place is Kameari!

436
00:25:51,980 --> 00:25:54,160
Well, surely it's Kameari!

437
00:25:55,260 --> 00:25:59,220
Everyone, come on over to our town!

438
00:26:00,080 --> 00:26:00,800
Thank you.

